{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794856972119,"sessionID":"ses_e1a303973ffeu6SRRIvgAvpDYA","part":{"partID":"prt_1e5cfec5c002J9hvA4jEoDoxYv","sessionID":"ses_e1a303973ffeu6SRRIvgAvpDYA","messageID":"msg_1e5cfcd3c001DiPNrNRX1xwCQD","type":"tool","id":"call_9285aeacdeb147249e35cfee","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-12.txt"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-12.txt, lines 1-10\n1: Code review pass twelve of command surfacing. Scope: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-scope-12.txt lists files as area TAB path. Your lineage label is the last folder of config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir: mention-12 reviews area mention, merged-12 reviews area merged. mention covers commandOnlyMentioned, which now drops a single quote that opens or closes a command name, keeps an apostrophe inside a word, and reads a retired command name beside the command it maps to, and the wrapper invariance test that checks every mention fixture reads the same wrapped in code, quote or bold marks, or under the retired name, as plain. Look for a wrapper, quote or alias case the invariance test does not cover and that changes a refusal or question into a request or back. merged covers the two merges of origin/main: sk-doc ROUTER.md and SKILL.md must equal main except the branch's README phrase narrowings and the /create:sk-skill command name, the generated intent signals must follow the router, and the doctor install contract test must check the presentation and the workflow against the link manifest.\n2: \n3: Cover all four dimensions (correctness, security, traceability, maintainability), and review every scope file of your area under at least two of them.\n4: \n5: Run each iteration as the deep-review workflow defines it, including its graph and stop steps, which earlier passes skipped:\n6: 1. Write the iteration record to your state log with dimensions, filesReviewed, findingsNew, newFindingsRatio and a graphEvents array: one dimension node per dimension you covered, one file node per file you read, one finding node per finding, one evidence node per finding naming its file:line, and edges COVERS (dimension to file), IN_DIMENSION and IN_FILE (finding to dimension and file) and EVIDENCE_FOR (evidence to finding). The shape is in .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-jsonl.md under Graph Events.\n7: 2. Persist them: node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs --spec-folder specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build --loop-type review --session-id <your config sessionId> --nodes '<json array>' --edges '<json array>', with kind and relation upper case.\n8: 3. Decide whether to stop: node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs --spec-folder specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build --loop-type review --session-id <your config sessionId> --convergence-mode default --stop-decision --config-path <absolute path of your deep-review-config.json> --state-log <absolute path of your deep-review-state.jsonl> --registry-path <absolute path of your deep-review-findings-registry.json> --iteration-count <iterations done> --security-sensitive-fix-scope false --fix-replay-required-rows 0 --fix-replay-passing-rows 0. Record its decision, stopReason and blockedBy in an event line of your state log. When the decision is STOP, synthesize and end with that stopReason; otherwise continue, aiming the next iteration at what blockedBy or the graph trace names.\n9: \n10: Do not re-report these recorded limits unless you show a new input that breaks them: a suffix followed by a file extension such as :auto.md reads as the command, as it did before this branch; a node -e arrow inside escaped quotes still reads as a redirect; isolation-check.sh is macOS only. Underscore emphasis around a command name is not dropped, because a command name may hold an underscore. The two moved baseline rows are judged without their text: 038-alignment-p1-remediation/scratch/lead-diag.mjs prints only lead indices. The open P2 list in 038-alignment-p1-remediation/scratch/alignment-final-dispositions.md and the open P2 of review passes ten and eleven (review-report-pass-10.md, review-report.md) are already recorded. The holdout gate is read by its count only, never its rows. Every finding is P0, P1 or P2 with file:line and a concrete input that shows it. HOLDOUT RULE: never open command-prompts.jsonl, holdout-prompts.jsonl or behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl except through jq 'del(.prompt)', never run git diff, show or log -p over a path that includes them without the pathspecs ':(exclude)**/command-prompts.jsonl' ':(exclude)**/holdout-prompts.jsonl' ':(exclude)**/behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl', never run score-command-transcripts.mjs --summary, and never print session text from a CLI session store. Never read or create .skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env. The reviewer changes no code; it writes only inside its lineage folder and through the two scripts above.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-12.txt, lines 1-10\n1: Code review pass twelve of command surfacing. Scope: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-scope-12.txt lists files as area TAB path. Your lineage label is the last folder of config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir: mention-12 reviews area mention, merged-12 reviews area merged. mention covers commandOnlyMentioned, which now drops a single quote that opens or closes a command name, keeps an apostrophe inside a word, and reads a retired command name beside the command it maps to, and the wrapper invariance test that checks every mention fixture reads the same wrapped in code, quote or bold marks, or under the retired name, as plain. Look for a wrapper, quote or alias case the invariance test does not cover and that changes a refusal or question into a request or back. merged covers the two merges of origin/main: sk-doc ROUTER.md and SKILL.md must equal main except the branch's README phrase narrowings and the /create:sk-skill command name, the generated intent signals must follow the router, and the doctor install contract test must check the presentation and the workflow against the link manifest.\n2: \n3: Cover all four dimensions (correctness, security, traceability, maintainability), and review every scope file of your area under at least two of them.\n4: \n5: Run each iteration as the deep-review workflow defines it, including its graph and stop steps, which earlier passes skipped:\n6: 1. Write the iteration record to your state log with dimensions, filesReviewed, findingsNew, newFindingsRatio and a graphEvents array: one dimension node per dimension you covered, one file node per file you read, one finding node per finding, one evidence node per finding naming its file:line, and edges COVERS (dimension to file), IN_DIMENSION and IN_FILE (finding to dimension and file) and EVIDENCE_FOR (evidence to finding). The shape is in .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-jsonl.md under Graph Events.\n7: 2. Persist them: node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs --spec-folder specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build --loop-type review --session-id <your config sessionId> --nodes '<json array>' --edges '<json array>', with kind and relation upper case.\n8: 3. Decide whether to stop: node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs --spec-folder specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build --loop-type review --session-id <your config sessionId> --convergence-mode default --stop-decision --config-path <absolute path of your deep-review-config.json> --state-log <absolute path of your deep-review-state.jsonl> --registry-path <absolute path of your deep-review-findings-registry.json> --iteration-count <iterations done> --security-sensitive-fix-scope false --fix-replay-required-rows 0 --fix-replay-passing-rows 0. Record its decision, stopReason and blockedBy in an event line of your state log. When the decision is STOP, synthesize and end with that stopReason; otherwise continue, aiming the next iteration at what blockedBy or the graph trace names.\n9: \n10: Do not re-report these recorded limits unless you show a new input that breaks them: a suffix followed by a file extension such as :auto.md reads as the command, as it did before this branch; a node -e arrow inside escaped quotes still reads as a redirect; isolation-check.sh is macOS only. Underscore emphasis around a command name is not dropped, because a command name may hold an underscore. The two moved baseline rows are judged without their text: 038-alignment-p1-remediation/scratch/lead-diag.mjs prints only lead indices. The open P2 list in 038-alignment-p1-remediation/scratch/alignment-final-dispositions.md and the open P2 of review passes ten and eleven (review-report-pass-10.md, review-report.md) are already recorded. The holdout gate is read by its count only, never its rows. Every finding is P0, P1 or P2 with file:line and a concrete input that shows it. HOLDOUT RULE: never open command-prompts.jsonl, holdout-prompts.jsonl or behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl except through jq 'del(.prompt)', never run git diff, show or log -p over a path that includes them without the pathspecs ':(exclude)**/command-prompts.jsonl' ':(exclude)**/holdout-prompts.jsonl' ':(exclude)**/behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl', never run score-command-transcripts.mjs --summary, and never print session text from a CLI session store. Never read or create .skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env. The reviewer changes no code; it writes only inside its lineage folder and through the two scripts above."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-12.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1794856971356,"end":1794856972119}}}}
