{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794857027331,"sessionID":"ses_e1a303973ffeu6SRRIvgAvpDYA","part":{"partID":"prt_1e5d0c485001wGb43yO83TWAYt","sessionID":"ses_e1a303973ffeu6SRRIvgAvpDYA","messageID":"msg_1e5d0bf79001YoPwCAHrr7X0si","type":"tool","id":"call_aff079745561488e92b0965d","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report.md, lines 1-31\n1: # Review Report: Command Surfacing Build, Pass Eleven (two lineages)\n2: \n3: - Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder)\n4: - Pass: the eleventh review pass. It read phase 039's sk-doc routing change and review pass ten's two fixes, `6d50afe6f39..2f3f893c153`, in two areas (`review/review-scope-11.txt`).\n5: - Executor: `cli-opencode` with `opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash` at reasoning effort max, cap eight iterations each, threshold 0.10, stop policy convergence, through `fanout-run.cjs` (exit 0). Brief `review/review-brief-11.txt`, config `review/deep-review-fanout-config-pass-11.json`. Pass ten's report is kept as `review-report-pass-10.md`.\n6: \n7: ## 1. Executive Summary\n8: \n9: - **Verdict: CONDITIONAL, both P1 fixed.** P0 0, P1 2, P2 10. Both P1 are fixed in phase 039 (T013), with a wrapper invariance test (T014) that pins the whole class: every mention fixture must read the same wrapped in code, quote or bold marks, and under a retired name, as it reads plain. Five P2 are fixed and five recorded.\n10: - **Stop.** routing-11 stopped at iteration 3 with `converged`. fixes-11 stopped at iteration 8 with `maxIterationsReached`, which is not convergence, so pass twelve reads these fixes.\n11: \n12: ## 2. Findings and Dispositions\n13: \n14: | Id | Severity | Location | Finding | Disposition |\n15: |----|----------|----------|---------|-------------|\n16: | FIX11-P1-001 | P1 | `lib/command-attach.ts` `commandOnlyMentioned` | A closing single quote after a command in an or-list hid the refusal for the later command | Fixed: a single quote that closes a command name is dropped too; the invariance test fails on the old code for straight and curly single quotes |\n17: | FIX11-P1-002 | P1 | `lib/command-attach.ts` `typedCommandForTop` | Refusing the retired `/create:skill` still delivered `/create:sk-skill` | Fixed: the mention check reads a retired name beside the command it maps to |\n18: | FIX11-P2-001 | P2 | `doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` | The test no longer checked the workflow its title names | Fixed: it asserts the workflow carries no stale offer sentence |\n19: | FIX11-P2-003 | P2 | `lib/command-attach.ts` comment | The comment named only the opening quote | Fixed with FIX11-P1-001 |\n20: | FIX11-P2-005 | P2 | `doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` | One assertion was subsumed by the next | Fixed: the subsumed line is gone |\n21: | F003 | P2 | 039 `spec.md` | The spec listed `sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md`, which was not changed | Fixed: row and scope mention removed |\n22: | F001 | P2 | `sk-doc/ROUTER.md` | The probe proves the hub only, and a dropped hook name loads the generic README template | Fixed in the docs: 039's purpose, REQ-003 and Known Limitations now say so |\n23: | F002 | P2 | `sk-doc/ROUTER.md` | The named skill-advisor hook phrase ties two README intents | Open, recorded |\n24: | F004 | P2 | `sk-doc/ROUTER.md` | Other named hooks bring the same cross-hub token class | Open, recorded |\n25: | F005 | P2 | `generate-router-intent-signals.cjs` | The carry rule and its check share a blind spot for dotted phrases | Open, recorded |\n26: | FIX11-P2-002 | P2 | 039 `acceptance-criteria.md` | AC-006 tests one instance of REQ-006 | Open, recorded: AC-007's invariance test now covers the class |\n27: | FIX11-P2-004 | P2 | `doctor-install-presentation.txt:78` | The sentence fuses the accepted list with the ones already there | Open, recorded |\n28: \n29: ## 3. Verification\n30: \n31: `039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/scratch/after-pass-eleven.txt` and `after-pass-eleven-invariance.txt`: build and typecheck exit 0, suite 0 failed with `AI_SESSION_CHILD` unset and set, doctor tests 1266 passed 0 failed, FLOOR 24/44 0/35 2/44, EVAL [160,49,21,5], stored sets unchanged.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report.md, lines 1-31\n1: # Review Report: Command Surfacing Build, Pass Eleven (two lineages)\n2: \n3: - Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder)\n4: - Pass: the eleventh review pass. It read phase 039's sk-doc routing change and review pass ten's two fixes, `6d50afe6f39..2f3f893c153`, in two areas (`review/review-scope-11.txt`).\n5: - Executor: `cli-opencode` with `opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash` at reasoning effort max, cap eight iterations each, threshold 0.10, stop policy convergence, through `fanout-run.cjs` (exit 0). Brief `review/review-brief-11.txt`, config `review/deep-review-fanout-config-pass-11.json`. Pass ten's report is kept as `review-report-pass-10.md`.\n6: \n7: ## 1. Executive Summary\n8: \n9: - **Verdict: CONDITIONAL, both P1 fixed.** P0 0, P1 2, P2 10. Both P1 are fixed in phase 039 (T013), with a wrapper invariance test (T014) that pins the whole class: every mention fixture must read the same wrapped in code, quote or bold marks, and under a retired name, as it reads plain. Five P2 are fixed and five recorded.\n10: - **Stop.** routing-11 stopped at iteration 3 with `converged`. fixes-11 stopped at iteration 8 with `maxIterationsReached`, which is not convergence, so pass twelve reads these fixes.\n11: \n12: ## 2. Findings and Dispositions\n13: \n14: | Id | Severity | Location | Finding | Disposition |\n15: |----|----------|----------|---------|-------------|\n16: | FIX11-P1-001 | P1 | `lib/command-attach.ts` `commandOnlyMentioned` | A closing single quote after a command in an or-list hid the refusal for the later command | Fixed: a single quote that closes a command name is dropped too; the invariance test fails on the old code for straight and curly single quotes |\n17: | FIX11-P1-002 | P1 | `lib/command-attach.ts` `typedCommandForTop` | Refusing the retired `/create:skill` still delivered `/create:sk-skill` | Fixed: the mention check reads a retired name beside the command it maps to |\n18: | FIX11-P2-001 | P2 | `doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` | The test no longer checked the workflow its title names | Fixed: it asserts the workflow carries no stale offer sentence |\n19: | FIX11-P2-003 | P2 | `lib/command-attach.ts` comment | The comment named only the opening quote | Fixed with FIX11-P1-001 |\n20: | FIX11-P2-005 | P2 | `doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` | One assertion was subsumed by the next | Fixed: the subsumed line is gone |\n21: | F003 | P2 | 039 `spec.md` | The spec listed `sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md`, which was not changed | Fixed: row and scope mention removed |\n22: | F001 | P2 | `sk-doc/ROUTER.md` | The probe proves the hub only, and a dropped hook name loads the generic README template | Fixed in the docs: 039's purpose, REQ-003 and Known Limitations now say so |\n23: | F002 | P2 | `sk-doc/ROUTER.md` | The named skill-advisor hook phrase ties two README intents | Open, recorded |\n24: | F004 | P2 | `sk-doc/ROUTER.md` | Other named hooks bring the same cross-hub token class | Open, recorded |\n25: | F005 | P2 | `generate-router-intent-signals.cjs` | The carry rule and its check share a blind spot for dotted phrases | Open, recorded |\n26: | FIX11-P2-002 | P2 | 039 `acceptance-criteria.md` | AC-006 tests one instance of REQ-006 | Open, recorded: AC-007's invariance test now covers the class |\n27: | FIX11-P2-004 | P2 | `doctor-install-presentation.txt:78` | The sentence fuses the accepted list with the ones already there | Open, recorded |\n28: \n29: ## 3. Verification\n30: \n31: `039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/scratch/after-pass-eleven.txt` and `after-pass-eleven-invariance.txt`: build and typecheck exit 0, suite 0 failed with `AI_SESSION_CHILD` unset and set, doctor tests 1266 passed 0 failed, FLOOR 24/44 0/35 2/44, EVAL [160,49,21,5], stored sets unchanged."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794857026693,"end":1794857027331}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794857027335,"sessionID":"ses_e1a303973ffeu6SRRIvgAvpDYA","part":{"partID":"prt_1e5d0c5b7001eoMUcLpsuvp4L6","sessionID":"ses_e1a303973ffeu6SRRIvgAvpDYA","messageID":"msg_1e5d0bf79001YoPwCAHrr7X0si","type":"tool","id":"call_6f10ea1f60a64d02970db669","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-10.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-10.md, lines 1-28\n1: # Review Report: Command Surfacing Build, Pass Ten (two lineages)\n2: \n3: - Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder)\n4: - Pass: the tenth review pass. It read the commits after pass nine (`05f776202e0..5b2b062baef`) and what the branch keeps over main in the merge `e91faf28b8c`, in two areas (`review/review-scope-10.txt`).\n5: - Executor: `cli-opencode` with `opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash` at reasoning effort max, cap eight iterations each, threshold 0.10, stop policy convergence, through `fanout-run.cjs` (exit 0). Brief `review/review-brief-10.txt`, config `review/deep-review-fanout-config-pass-10.json`. Pass nine's report is kept as `review-report-pass-9.md`.\n6: \n7: ## 1. Executive Summary\n8: \n9: - **Verdict: CONDITIONAL, both P1 fixed.** P0 0, P1 2, P2 7. Both P1 and three P2 are fixed in phase 039 (T010, T011). Four P2 are recorded as open.\n10: - **Stop.** attach-scorer-10 stopped at iteration 7 with `converged`. docs-merge-10 stopped at iteration 5 with `stuckRecovery`, which is not convergence, so a further pass reads phase 039 and these fixes.\n11: \n12: ## 2. Findings and Dispositions\n13: \n14: | Id | Severity | Location | Finding | Disposition |\n15: |----|----------|----------|---------|-------------|\n16: | AC10-P1-001 | P1 | `lib/command-attach.ts` `commandOnlyMentioned` | A single-quoted command name still hid a refusal or question lead | Fixed: a single quote that opens a command name is dropped, contractions keep theirs; three cases fail without it |\n17: | F001 | P1 | `doctor-install-presentation.txt:78` | The merge took main's runtime sentence while the branch's contract test and workflow still said DSH is not offered | Fixed: the presentation names the eight manifest runtimes, the stale DSH sentence is gone, the test reads the manifest |\n18: | F002 | P2 | `doctor-install-presentation.txt:78` | The sentence said nine but listed eight | Fixed with F001 |\n19: | AC10-P2-002 | P2 | `lib/command-attach.ts` | The curly double quotes had no test | Fixed: case added |\n20: | AC10-P2-003 | P2 | `lib/command-attach.ts` | The comment did not say why the apostrophe stays | Fixed: the comment names it |\n21: | AC10-P2-001 | P2 | `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` | The in-any-order clause of the suffix requirement has no test | Open, recorded |\n22: | F003 | P2 | advisor `README.md:244` | The runtime lists leave out Vibe | Open, recorded (the final alignment run's B3 too) |\n23: | F004 | P2 | `changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:44` | The no-edit bullet claims more than the gate | Open, recorded |\n24: | F005 | P2 | `changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:102` | The suffix list is narrower than the parser | Open, recorded |\n25: \n26: ## 3. Verification\n27: \n28: `039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/scratch/after-pass-ten.txt`: build and typecheck exit 0, suite 2353 passed 0 failed with `AI_SESSION_CHILD` unset and set, FLOOR 24/44 0/35 2/44, EVAL [160,49,21,5], stored sets unchanged. Doctor script tests 1266 passed 0 failed.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-10.md, lines 1-28\n1: # Review Report: Command Surfacing Build, Pass Ten (two lineages)\n2: \n3: - Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder)\n4: - Pass: the tenth review pass. It read the commits after pass nine (`05f776202e0..5b2b062baef`) and what the branch keeps over main in the merge `e91faf28b8c`, in two areas (`review/review-scope-10.txt`).\n5: - Executor: `cli-opencode` with `opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash` at reasoning effort max, cap eight iterations each, threshold 0.10, stop policy convergence, through `fanout-run.cjs` (exit 0). Brief `review/review-brief-10.txt`, config `review/deep-review-fanout-config-pass-10.json`. Pass nine's report is kept as `review-report-pass-9.md`.\n6: \n7: ## 1. Executive Summary\n8: \n9: - **Verdict: CONDITIONAL, both P1 fixed.** P0 0, P1 2, P2 7. Both P1 and three P2 are fixed in phase 039 (T010, T011). Four P2 are recorded as open.\n10: - **Stop.** attach-scorer-10 stopped at iteration 7 with `converged`. docs-merge-10 stopped at iteration 5 with `stuckRecovery`, which is not convergence, so a further pass reads phase 039 and these fixes.\n11: \n12: ## 2. Findings and Dispositions\n13: \n14: | Id | Severity | Location | Finding | Disposition |\n15: |----|----------|----------|---------|-------------|\n16: | AC10-P1-001 | P1 | `lib/command-attach.ts` `commandOnlyMentioned` | A single-quoted command name still hid a refusal or question lead | Fixed: a single quote that opens a command name is dropped, contractions keep theirs; three cases fail without it |\n17: | F001 | P1 | `doctor-install-presentation.txt:78` | The merge took main's runtime sentence while the branch's contract test and workflow still said DSH is not offered | Fixed: the presentation names the eight manifest runtimes, the stale DSH sentence is gone, the test reads the manifest |\n18: | F002 | P2 | `doctor-install-presentation.txt:78` | The sentence said nine but listed eight | Fixed with F001 |\n19: | AC10-P2-002 | P2 | `lib/command-attach.ts` | The curly double quotes had no test | Fixed: case added |\n20: | AC10-P2-003 | P2 | `lib/command-attach.ts` | The comment did not say why the apostrophe stays | Fixed: the comment names it |\n21: | AC10-P2-001 | P2 | `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` | The in-any-order clause of the suffix requirement has no test | Open, recorded |\n22: | F003 | P2 | advisor `README.md:244` | The runtime lists leave out Vibe | Open, recorded (the final alignment run's B3 too) |\n23: | F004 | P2 | `changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:44` | The no-edit bullet claims more than the gate | Open, recorded |\n24: | F005 | P2 | `changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:102` | The suffix list is narrower than the parser | Open, recorded |\n25: \n26: ## 3. Verification\n27: \n28: `039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/scratch/after-pass-ten.txt`: build and typecheck exit 0, suite 2353 passed 0 failed with `AI_SESSION_CHILD` unset and set, FLOOR 24/44 0/35 2/44, EVAL [160,49,21,5], stored sets unchanged. Doctor script tests 1266 passed 0 failed."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-10.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794857026999,"end":1794857027335}}}}
