ew/lineages/accuracy-runner-2/iterations/iteration-004.md:18:- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:1-130`\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-2/iterations/iteration-004.md:20:- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/README.md:100-165`\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-2/iterations/iteration-004.md:24:- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md:170-180,250-280`\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-2/iterations/iteration-004.md:52:3. **`runtime/tests/README.md` describes the playbook inventory test as a routing-fixture test** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/README.md:154` -- The key-files table says `manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts` \"Verifies manual testing playbook routing fixtures.\" The test does not touch routing fixtures: it parses the root playbook's scenario rows, compares them with the live per-feature file list, and asserts the 50-row/50-file inventory and the two \"50 scenario files\" sentences (`manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts:43-79`). A reader who trusts the table will look for routing coverage in a test that has none, and will miss the test that would catch a playbook inventory drift.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-2/iterations/iteration-004.md:55:Affected surface hints: `runtime/tests/README.md:154`; `manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts`; the file's own `describe` text at line 43.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-2/iterations/iteration-004.md:58:4. **The scorer README says `--row-id` narrows either mode, but single-session mode ignores it** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:112` -- The row for `score-command-transcripts.mjs` says \"`--row-id <id>` narrows either mode to one row\". In `--runtime --locator` mode the flag is parsed (`score-command-transcripts.mjs:92-95`) and then never read: `main` calls `scoreSession(options)` (line 1455), and `scoreSession` reads only `options.locator`, `options.runtime` and `options.json` (lines 885-901). The mode's output is a record count for one session, so a row filter has nothing to narrow, and the flag is silently accepted. The usage line repeats the claim (`:40`).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-2/iterations/iteration-004.md:61:Affected surface hints: `README.md:40,112`; `score-command-transcripts.mjs` `parseArgs` and `scoreSession`; any operator who passes `--row-id` expecting a per-row session score.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-2/iterations/iteration-004.md:88:- `score-command-transcripts.mjs` ↔ `README.md`: the usage text and the flag parser agree on accepting `--row-id` in both modes, and the session-mode body is where the promise stops.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-2/iterations/iteration-004.md:96:- **No shared-doc contradiction was invented.** `system-skill-advisor/README.md` and `ARCHITECTURE.md` describe the bench, the playbook and the test surfaces accurately for this area; only the four findings above disagree with their code or tree.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-2/iterations/iteration-005.md:20:- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:100-125`\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-2/iterations/iteration-005.md:62:- `score-command-transcripts.mjs` 