{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794857452903,"sessionID":"ses_e1a303973ffeu6SRRIvgAvpDYA","part":{"partID":"prt_1e5d74371002ZdJ0kRsXjUitnS","sessionID":"ses_e1a303973ffeu6SRRIvgAvpDYA","messageID":"msg_1e5d73cea001AbzymXS7ZznMb5","type":"tool","id":"call_12c7ac343d8646a981f5d4fd","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":120,"offset":1690,"path":".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs"},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs, lines 1690-1809\n1690:           `review_target: ${options.reviewTarget || specFolder}`,\n1691:           `review_target_type: ${options.reviewTargetType || 'spec-folder'}`,\n1692:           `review_dimensions: all`,\n1693:           ...(reviewFocus ? [`review_focus: ${reviewFocus}`] : []),\n1694:           `spec_folder: ${specFolder}`,\n1695:           `execution_mode: AUTONOMOUS`,\n1696:           `lineage_mode: auto`,\n1697:           ``,\n1698:         ]\n1699:       : [];\n1700:   const prompt = [\n1701:     `GATE 3 IS PRE-RESOLVED. DO NOT ASK THE DOCUMENTATION-SCOPE QUESTION.`,\n1702:     `You are a non-interactive dispatched worker: AI_SESSION_CHILD=1 is set, which AGENTS.md defines as the autonomous child-dispatch exemption. Nobody is at a prompt, so no answer can reach you.`,\n1703:     `Your write authority is already bound to ${promptDir}. The dispatcher's answer to every other stop-and-ask rule (Halt Conditions, Logic-Sync, stop-for-yes): follow the workflow within this prompt's write limits, record the conflict in the current iteration, and continue. Never end a turn with a question or A/B/C/D options.`,\n1704:     `A failed call means re-check the path and retry; halt only after three failures on the same call. The lineage is complete only when its files exist on disk and the completion line below is printed.`,\n1705:     ``,\n1706:     `You are orchestrating the ${agentName} workflow YAML as a detached fan-out lineage.`,\n1707:     ...detachedIntro,\n1708:     ``,\n1709:     ...inProcessDirective,\n1710:     ...(lineage.kind !== 'native'\n1711:       ? [agentPersonaBlock(agentName, path.resolve(__dirname, '../../../../../'))]\n1712:       : []),\n1713:     ...leafContract,\n1714:     `Read ${skillFile} and execute the ${loopType} loop with these parameters:`,\n1715:     ...params,\n1716:     ...setupBindings,\n1717:     `The step_resolve_artifact_root step will bind artifact_dir to ${lineageDir} via the`,\n1718:     `config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir override — do NOT run the resolveArtifactRoot node`,\n1719:     `command; bind artifact_dir directly to the override value.`,\n1720:     ``,\n1721:     `Run phase_init, phase_main_loop (${stopClause}), and phase_synthesis.`,\n1722:     `Write EVERY file you create or modify inside ${promptDir} and nowhere else — that directory is`,\n1723:     `your entire write surface. Its absolute path is ${absoluteLineageDir}; the`,\n1724:     `relative form is resolved from the repository root, so a path that drops the leading`,\n1725:     `directories (for example one starting with review/ or research/) lands OUTSIDE the lineage and`,\n1726:     `fails it. You may read anywhere, but do NOT modify, create, or delete any file`,\n1727:     `outside ${promptDir}, and do NOT run any command that writes outside it: in particular do NOT`,\n1728:     `run generate-context.js, validate.sh (especially --recursive), or any git write/checkout/commit`,\n1729:     `command. Producing findings does not mean running the repo's tooling — a single out-of-scope`,\n1730:     `write fails this whole lineage.`,\n1731:     `Use the repository-relative form ${promptDir} in every tool call, copied character for character; never type the absolute home prefix or rebuild the path from the packet or track name.`,\n1732:     `A \"file not found\" on a path you just wrote means the path was mistyped: re-copy ${promptDir} and retry.`,\n1733:     // A CLI lineage runs every iteration from this one prompt, so a lead's review file reaches\n1734:     // later iterations only when the prompt names it. Native lineages receive a different input.\n1735:     ...(lineage.kind !== 'native'\n1736:       ? [\n1737:           `Before init, before each iteration, and before resolving any conflict, read ${path.join(promptDir, 'steer.md')} when it exists.`,\n1738:           `It is the lead's channel: its rulings are the dispatcher's answers to questions this lineage would otherwise ask, and they bind inside the lineage directory.`,\n1739:           `It grants no write outside the lineage. When you read it, list it among that iteration's sources.`,\n1740:         ]\n1741:       : []),\n1742:     ...(hasIterationCap && stopPolicy === 'max-iterations'\n1743:       ? [\n1744:           `The terminal synthesis record must carry stopReason \"maxIterationsReached\"; the runner`,\n1745:           `rejects a lineage whose synthesis reaches the cap without recording that reason.`,\n1746:         ]\n1747:       : []),\n1748:     ``,\n1749:     `When complete, output a single line: FANOUT_LINEAGE_COMPLETE:${lineage.label}`,\n1750:   ].join('\\n');\n1751:   return prompt;\n1752: }\n1753: \n1754: function buildNativeCommandInput(loopType, specFolder, lineageDir, lineage, options = {}) {\n1755:   assertActiveFanoutLoopType(loopType);\n1756:   const maxIterations = lineage.iterations || 12;\n1757:   const convergenceThreshold = options.convergenceThreshold ?? (loopType === 'research' ? 0.05 : 0.1);\n1758:   const stopPolicy = options.stopPolicy || 'convergence';\n1759:   const sessionId = options.sessionId || '';\n1760:   const reviewTarget = loopType === 'review' && options.reviewTarget ? options.reviewTarget : specFolder;\n1761:   const reviewTargetType = loopType === 'review' && options.reviewTargetType\n1762:     ? options.reviewTargetType\n1763:     : 'spec-folder';\n1764:   const args = [\n1765:     ':auto',\n1766:     JSON.stringify(loopType === 'review' ? reviewTarget : specFolder),\n