{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794857495319,"sessionID":"ses_e1a303973ffeu6SRRIvgAvpDYA","part":{"partID":"prt_1e5d7e96f001ZgEekGzkpqtOUl","sessionID":"ses_e1a303973ffeu6SRRIvgAvpDYA","messageID":"msg_1e5d7d6f0001MSOyivLI7W4dZ1","type":"tool","id":"call_9251bdb4559b4785aaa0b451","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":200,"offset":2076,"path":".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml"},"output":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml, lines 2076-2275\n2076: \n2077:           5. **Spec Seed**\n2078:              - Concrete seed bullets for follow-on spec updates\n2079: \n2080:           6. **Plan Seed**\n2081:              - Concrete starter tasks for `/speckit:plan`\n2082: \n2083:            7. **Traceability Status**\n2084:               - Summarize required core protocols first, then applicable overlay protocols\n2085:               - Include status, evidence, and any unresolved drift per protocol\n2086:               - Include `AC_COVERAGE` status for lifecycle-active spec-folder targets: exempt, disabled, pass, or advisory-shortfall, with covered/total and floor when available\n2087: \n2088:           If `resource_map_present` is true, insert **## Resource Map Coverage Gate** after `Traceability Status` with exactly three bullets:\n2089:              - `Entries touched`: count of resource-map paths that appear in applied reports\n2090:              - `Entries not touched`: paths in resource-map not in implementation, labeled `expected-by-scope` or `gap`\n2091:              - `Implementation paths absent from resource-map`: `target_files` in applied reports not on the map\n2092: \n2093:           8. **Deferred Items**\n2094:              - Advisory-only or backlog-worthy follow-ups that do not block the current verdict\n2095: \n2096:           **Dimension Expansion Map**\n2097:              - Insert `## Dimension Expansion Map` after Deferred Items and before Search Ledger.\n2098:              - Render reducer-owned `divergence.saturatedDirections`, completed pivots, failed pivots, audited overrides, Council artifact references, selected review directions, and remaining frontier.\n2099:              - This section records breadth only. It cannot alter the Executive Summary verdict, hasAdvisories, finding registry, or adversarial self-check results.\n2100: \n2101:           9. **Search Ledger**\n2102:              - Always include this section before the appendix.\n2103:              - Render reducer-owned `searchCoverage`, `candidateCoverage`, `searchDebt`, `ruledOutCandidates`, and `cleanSearchProof`.\n2104:              - If all arrays are empty or absent, include: `*No search-depth state captured (legacy v1 record)*`.\n2105:              - When `searchDebt` is non-empty, state hasSearchDebt: true. The verdict already counts it: CONDITIONAL unless an active P0 or a failed gate makes it FAIL. When debt is the only reason for CONDITIONAL, the next step is another /deep:review over the deferred or blocked bug classes, not /speckit:plan.\n2106: \n2107:           10. **Audit Appendix**\n2108:              - Convergence summary, coverage summary, ruled-out claims, sources reviewed\n2109:              - Cross-reference appendix MUST be split into `Core Protocols` and `Overlay Protocols`\n2110: \n2111:           Preserve machine-owned markers so the reducer-owned registry, dashboard, and strategy anchors can be refreshed on re-run without mutating prior synthesis. (Note: `completed-continue` lineage branch is deferred — see `deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches`.)\n2112:         output: \"{state_paths.review_output}\"\n2113: \n2114:       step_derive_release_readiness_state:\n2115:         action: \"Bind release-readiness state from final review results\"\n2116:         algorithm: |\n2117:           if active_p0 > 0:\n2118:             release_readiness_state = \"release-blocking\"\n2119:           elif reason == \"converged\" and verdict in [\"PASS\", \"CONDITIONAL\"]:\n2120:             release_readiness_state = \"converged\"\n2121:           else:\n2122:             release_readiness_state = \"in-progress\"\n2123:         outputs:\n2124:           - release_readiness_state: \"in-progress | converged | release-blocking\"\n2125:         note: \"State meanings follow releaseReadinessStates in deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml.\"\n2126: \n2127:       step_convergence_report:\n2128:         action: \"Append convergence report to JSONL\"\n2129:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2130:         command: |\n2131:           GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n2132:           [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n2133:           EVENT_DIR=\"$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-synthesis.XXXXXX\")\"\n2134:           CLOSEOUT=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/synthesis-closeout.cjs\"\n2135:           [ -f \"$CLOSEOUT\" ] || CLOSEOUT=\"scripts/synthesis-closeout.cjs\"\n2136:           node \"$CLOSEOUT\" --mode review --event-dir \"$EVENT_DIR\" \\\n2137:             --artifact-dir \"{state_paths.packet_dir}\" \\\n2138:             --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\" \\\n2139:             --registry \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\" \\\n2140:             --output \"{state_paths.review_output}\" \\\n2141:             --dashboard \"{state_paths.dashboard}\" \\\n2142:             --stop-reason \"{reason}\" \\\n2143:             --active-p0 \"{active_p0}\" --active-p1 \"{active_p1}\" --active-p2 \"{active_p2}\" \\\n2144:             --dimension-coverage \"{dimension_coverage}\" \\\n2145:             --verdict \"{verdict}\" \\\n2146:             --release-readiness-state \"{release_readiness_state}\"\n2147:           NODE_STATUS=$?\n2148:           for eventFile in \"$EVENT_DIR\"/*.json; do\n2149:             [ -e \"$eventFile\" ] || continue\n2150:             node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$eventFile\"\n2151:             GATEWAY_STATUS=$?\n2152:             if [ \"$GATEWAY_STATUS\" -ne 0 ]; then\n2153:               rm -rf \"$EVENT_DIR\"\n2154:               exit \"$GATEWAY_STATUS\"\n2155:             fi\n2156:           done\n2157:           rm -rf \"$EVENT_DIR\"\n2158:           exit \"$NODE_STATUS\"\n2159:         note: \"Emit as numeric ratio (e.g., 0.75), not quoted string. Compute: dimensions_covered / total_dimensions.\"\n2160: \n2161:       step_update_config_status:\n2162:         action: \"Mark config as complete\"\n2163:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2164:         edit: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n2165:         set_field: { status: \"complete\" }\n2166: \n2167:       step_stage_artifact_dir:\n2168:         skip_when: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is present\"\n2169:         action: \"Stage all skill-owned artifacts under artifact_dir for the operator's next git commit\"\n2170:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2171:         command: \"git add {state_paths.artifact_dir}\"\n2172:         note: \"Staging the whole artifact_dir keeps the iteration trail (iterations/, deltas/, state.jsonl, strategy, findings-registry, and the report) together; the operator keeps commit authority and can `git restore --staged {path}` before committing. Failure is non-fatal -- log warning and continue.\"\n2173:         on_fail: \"Log warning. Do not block synthesis. The artifact_dir may be outside a git repo (e.g., temp test fixture) which is a valid case.\"\n2174: \n2175:       # ─── APPROVAL GATE: Post-Synthesis ───\n2176:       gate_post_synthesis:\n2177:         applies_to: confirm\n2178:         type: approval_gate\n2179:         purpose: \"Show review/review-report.md summary and get approval\"\n2180:         present: |\n2181:           ## Review Synthesis Complete\n2182: \n2183:           **review/review-report.md** has been compiled with findings from {iteration_count} iterations.\n2184:           **Verdict**: {verdict} | **hasAdvisories**: {has_advisories}\n2185:           **Active Findings**: P0={active_p0} P1={active_p1} P2={active_p2}\n2186:           **Dimension Coverage**: {dimension_coverage}\n2187: \n2188:           Review `{state_paths.review_output}` before deciding next steps.\n2189: \n2190:           Options:\n2191:           A) Approve and save to memory\n2192:           B) Generate remediation plan (creates action items for /speckit:plan)\n2193:           C) Request revisions to review/review-report.md\n2194:           D) Skip memory save\n2195:         wait_for: \"User response\"\n2196:         after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n2197:         on_A: { proceed_to: phase_save }\n2198:         on_B: { action: \"Generate remediation plan section, then save to memory\", proceed_to: phase_save }\n2199:         on_C: { action: \"Apply user revisions\", return_to: gate_post_synthesis }\n2200:         on_D: { proceed_to: completion }\n2201: \n2202:   # ════════\n2203:   # PHASE 4: SAVE\n2204:   # ════════\n2205:   phase_save:\n2206:     purpose: Preserve review context in packet continuity\n2207:     steps:\n2208: \n2209:       step_compose_save_payload:\n2210:         action: \"Compose the structured JSON payload consumed by generate-context.js\"\n2211:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2212:         output: \"/tmp/save-context-data-<session-id>.json\"\n2213:         requirements:\n2214:           - \"Write this file before invoking generate-context.js; the loader fails closed if the explicit JSON file is absent.\"\n2215:           - \"Include `specFolder`, a concise `sessionSummary`, curated `observations`, `recent_context`, `toolCalls`, and `exchanges` from the completed review loop. Without `--full-auto` the writer only plans, and a full-auto save writes continuity only from `recent_action`, `next_safe_action`, `blockers` and `key_files`, so the payload carries all four.\"\n2216:           - \"Use a session-scoped temp filename; do not use the retired shared `/tmp/save-context-data.json` path.\"\n2217:         example_payload: |\n2218:           {\n2219:             \"specFolder\": \"{spec_folder}\",\n2220:             \"sessionSummary\": \"Deep review completed; see review/review-report.md for verdict, findings, and workstreams.\",\n2221:             \"observations\": [\"Summarize the active findings, verdict, and remediation guidance.\"],\n2222:             \"recent_context\": [\"Point to the generated review artifacts and next action.\"],\n2223:             \"exchanges\": [],\n2224:             \"toolCalls\": [],\n2225:             \"recent_action\": \"Deep review finished with verdict {verdict} after {iteration_count} iterations\",\n2226:             \"next_safe_action\": \"Act on the verdict in review/review-report.md\",\n2227:             \"blockers\": [],\n2228:             \"key_files\": [\"review/review-report.md\"]\n2229:           }\n2230: \n2231:       step_generate_context:\n2232:         action: \"Route continuity content into the correct canonical spec document via generate-context.js\"\n2233:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2234:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js /tmp/save-context-data-<session-id>.json {spec_folder} --full-auto\"\n2235:         critical_rule: \"NEVER manually author files under retired memory/ paths (the runtime rejects them); use generate-context.js so the save routes into decision-record.md, implementation-summary.md, or handover.md\"\n2236: \n2237:       step_verify_save:\n2238:         action: \"Verify canonical save routed content into the correct spec document\"\n2239:         check: \"Does {spec_folder}/implementation-summary.md, {spec_folder}/decision-record.md, or {spec_folder}/handover.md carry the new continuity update?\"\n2240:         on_fail: \"Log warning but do not block completion\"\n2241: \n2242:       step_release_lock:\n2243:         action: \"Release the single-writer lock after save, skip-save, or cancellation cleanup has resolved\"\n2244:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2245:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}\"\n2246:         bookkeeping_log: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"lock_released\",\"path\":\"{state_paths.lock_file}\",\"releasePhase\":\"save\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n2247: \n2248:   # ════════\n2249:   # COMPLETION\n2250:   # ════════\n2251:   completion:\n2252:     message: |\n2253:       Deep review complete.\n2254:       Iterations: {iteration_count} | Stop reason: {reason}\n2255:       Findings: P0={active_p0} P1={active_p1} P2={active_p2}\n2256:       Verdict: {verdict} | hasAdvisories={has_advisories}\n2257: \n2258:       Artifacts:\n2259:         - review/review-report.md (compiled from {iteration_count} iterations)\n2260:         - {iteration_count} iteration files in review/iterations/\n2261:         - State files in review/: deep-review-config.json, deep-review-state.jsonl, deep-review-findings-registry.json, deep-review-strategy.md, deep-review-dashboard.md\n2262:         - Memory context saved\n2263: \n2264:       STATUS=OK PATH={spec_folder}\n2265:     next_steps:\n2266:       - \"/speckit:plan [remediation] (if FAIL or CONDITIONAL verdict)\"\n2267:       - \"/create:changelog (if PASS, including PASS with hasAdvisories=true)\"\n2268:       - \"/deep:review [target] (for another review)\"\n2269:       - \"/speckit:save {spec_folder} (refresh canonical continuity before the next session)\"\n2270: \n2271: # ────────\n2272: # ERROR RECOVERY\n2273: # ────────\n2274: error_recovery:\n2275:   agent_dispatch_timeout: \"Retry once with reduced scope (fewer files per iteration). If second timeout, mark as 'timeout' and continue.\"\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 2276]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml, lines 2076-2275\n2076: \n2077:           5. **Spec Seed**\n2078:              - Concrete seed bullets for follow-on spec updates\n2079: \n2080:           6. **Plan Seed**\n2081:              - Concrete starter tasks for `/speckit:plan`\n2082: \n2083:            7. **Traceability Status**\n2084:               - Summarize required core protocols first, then applicable overlay protocols\n2085:               - Include status, evidence, and any unresolved drift per protocol\n2086:               - Include `AC_COVERAGE` status for lifecycle-active spec-folder targets: exempt, disabled, pass, or advisory-shortfall, with covered/total and floor when available\n2087: \n2088:           If `resource_map_present` is true, insert **## Resource Map Coverage Gate** after `Traceability Status` with exactly three bullets:\n2089:              - `Entries touched`: count of resource-map paths that appear in applied reports\n2090:              - `Entries not touched`: paths in resource-map not in implementation, labeled `expected-by-scope` or `gap`\n2091:              - `Implementation paths absent from resource-map`: `target_files` in applied reports not on the map\n2092: \n2093:           8. **Deferred Items**\n2094:              - Advisory-only or backlog-worthy follow-ups that do not block the current verdict\n2095: \n2096:           **Dimension Expansion Map**\n2097:              - Insert `## Dimension Expansion Map` after Deferred Items and before Search Ledger.\n2098:              - Render reducer-owned `divergence.saturatedDirections`, completed pivots, failed pivots, audited overrides, Council artifact references, selected review directions, and remaining frontier.\n2099:              - This section records breadth only. It cannot alter the Executive Summary verdict, hasAdvisories, finding registry, or adversarial self-check results.\n2100: \n2101:           9. **Search Ledger**\n2102:              - Always include this section before the appendix.\n2103:              - Render reducer-owned `searchCoverage`, `candidateCoverage`, `searchDebt`, `ruledOutCandidates`, and `cleanSearchProof`.\n2104:              - If all arrays are empty or absent, include: `*No search-depth state captured (legacy v1 record)*`.\n2105:              - When `searchDebt` is non-empty, state hasSearchDebt: true. The verdict already counts it: CONDITIONAL unless an active P0 or a failed gate makes it FAIL. When debt is the only reason for CONDITIONAL, the next step is another /deep:review over the deferred or blocked bug classes, not /speckit:plan.\n2106: \n2107:           10. **Audit Appendix**\n2108:              - Convergence summary, coverage summary, ruled-out claims, sources reviewed\n2109:              - Cross-reference appendix MUST be split into `Core Protocols` and `Overlay Protocols`\n2110: \n2111:           Preserve machine-owned markers so the reducer-owned registry, dashboard, and strategy anchors can be refreshed on re-run without mutating prior synthesis. (Note: `completed-continue` lineage branch is deferred — see `deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches`.)\n2112:         output: \"{state_paths.review_output}\"\n2113: \n2114:       step_derive_release_readiness_state:\n2115:         action: \"Bind release-readiness state from final review results\"\n2116:         algorithm: |\n2117:           if active_p0 > 0:\n2118:             release_readiness_state = \"release-blocking\"\n2119:           elif reason == \"converged\" and verdict in [\"PASS\", \"CONDITIONAL\"]:\n2120:             release_readiness_state = \"converged\"\n2121:           else:\n2122:             release_readiness_state = \"in-progress\"\n2123:         outputs:\n2124:           - release_readiness_state: \"in-progress | converged | release-blocking\"\n2125:         note: \"State meanings follow releaseReadinessStates in deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml.\"\n2126: \n2127:       step_convergence_report:\n2128:         action: \"Append convergence report to JSONL\"\n2129:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2130:         command: |\n2131:           GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n2132:           [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n2133:           EVENT_DIR=\"$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-synthesis.XXXXXX\")\"\n2134:           CLOSEOUT=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/synthesis-closeout.cjs\"\n2135:           [ -f \"$CLOSEOUT\" ] || CLOSEOUT=\"scripts/synthesis-closeout.cjs\"\n2136:           node \"$CLOSEOUT\" --mode review --event-dir \"$EVENT_DIR\" \\\n2137:             --artifact-dir \"{state_paths.packet_dir}\" \\\n2138:             --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\" \\\n2139:             --registry \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\" \\\n2140:             --output \"{state_paths.review_output}\" \\\n2141:             --dashboard \"{state_paths.dashboard}\" \\\n2142:             --stop-reason \"{reason}\" \\\n2143:             --active-p0 \"{active_p0}\" --active-p1 \"{active_p1}\" --active-p2 \"{active_p2}\" \\\n2144:             --dimension-coverage \"{dimension_coverage}\" \\\n2145:             --verdict \"{verdict}\" \\\n2146:             --release-readiness-state \"{release_readiness_state}\"\n2147:           NODE_STATUS=$?\n2148:           for eventFile in \"$EVENT_DIR\"/*.json; do\n2149:             [ -e \"$eventFile\" ] || continue\n2150:             node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$eventFile\"\n2151:             GATEWAY_STATUS=$?\n2152:             if [ \"$GATEWAY_STATUS\" -ne 0 ]; then\n2153:               rm -rf \"$EVENT_DIR\"\n2154:               exit \"$GATEWAY_STATUS\"\n2155:             fi\n2156:           done\n2157:           rm -rf \"$EVENT_DIR\"\n2158:           exit \"$NODE_STATUS\"\n2159:         note: \"Emit as numeric ratio (e.g., 0.75), not quoted string. Compute: dimensions_covered / total_dimensions.\"\n2160: \n2161:       step_update_config_status:\n2162:         action: \"Mark config as complete\"\n2163:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2164:         edit: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n2165:         set_field: { status: \"complete\" }\n2166: \n2167:       step_stage_artifact_dir:\n2168:         skip_when: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is present\"\n2169:         action: \"Stage all skill-owned artifacts under artifact_dir for the operator's next git commit\"\n2170:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2171:         command: \"git add {state_paths.artifact_dir}\"\n2172:         note: \"Staging the whole artifact_dir keeps the iteration trail (iterations/, deltas/, state.jsonl, strategy, findings-registry, and the report) together; the operator keeps commit authority and can `git restore --staged {path}` before committing. Failure is non-fatal -- log warning and continue.\"\n2173:         on_fail: \"Log warning. Do not block synthesis. The artifact_dir may be outside a git repo (e.g., temp test fixture) which is a valid case.\"\n2174: \n2175:       # ─── APPROVAL GATE: Post-Synthesis ───\n2176:       gate_post_synthesis:\n2177:         applies_to: confirm\n2178:         type: approval_gate\n2179:         purpose: \"Show review/review-report.md summary and get approval\"\n2180:         present: |\n2181:           ## Review Synthesis Complete\n2182: \n2183:           **review/review-report.md** has been compiled with findings from {iteration_count} iterations.\n2184:           **Verdict**: {verdict} | **hasAdvisories**: {has_advisories}\n2185:           **Active Findings**: P0={active_p0} P1={active_p1} P2={active_p2}\n2186:           **Dimension Coverage**: {dimension_coverage}\n2187: \n2188:           Review `{state_paths.review_output}` before deciding next steps.\n2189: \n2190:           Options:\n2191:           A) Approve and save to memory\n2192:           B) Generate remediation plan (creates action items for /speckit:plan)\n2193:           C) Request revisions to review/review-report.md\n2194:           D) Skip memory save\n2195:         wait_for: \"User response\"\n2196:         after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n2197:         on_A: { proceed_to: phase_save }\n2198:         on_B: { action: \"Generate remediation plan section, then save to memory\", proceed_to: phase_save }\n2199:         on_C: { action: \"Apply user revisions\", return_to: gate_post_synthesis }\n2200:         on_D: { proceed_to: completion }\n2201: \n2202:   # ════════\n2203:   # PHASE 4: SAVE\n2204:   # ════════\n2205:   phase_save:\n2206:     purpose: Preserve review context in packet continuity\n2207:     steps:\n2208: \n2209:       step_compose_save_payload:\n2210:         action: \"Compose the structured JSON payload consumed by generate-context.js\"\n2211:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2212:         output: \"/tmp/save-context-data-<session-id>.json\"\n2213:         requirements:\n2214:           - \"Write this file before invoking generate-context.js; the loader fails closed if the explicit JSON file is absent.\"\n2215:           - \"Include `specFolder`, a concise `sessionSummary`, curated `observations`, `recent_context`, `toolCalls`, and `exchanges` from the completed review loop. Without `--full-auto` the writer only plans, and a full-auto save writes continuity only from `recent_action`, `next_safe_action`, `blockers` and `key_files`, so the payload carries all four.\"\n2216:           - \"Use a session-scoped temp filename; do not use the retired shared `/tmp/save-context-data.json` path.\"\n2217:         example_payload: |\n2218:           {\n2219:             \"specFolder\": \"{spec_folder}\",\n2220:             \"sessionSummary\": \"Deep review completed; see review/review-report.md for verdict, findings, and workstreams.\",\n2221:             \"observations\": [\"Summarize the active findings, verdict, and remediation guidance.\"],\n2222:             \"recent_context\": [\"Point to the generated review artifacts and next action.\"],\n2223:             \"exchanges\": [],\n2224:             \"toolCalls\": [],\n2225:             \"recent_action\": \"Deep review finished with verdict {verdict} after {iteration_count} iterations\",\n2226:             \"next_safe_action\": \"Act on the verdict in review/review-report.md\",\n2227:             \"blockers\": [],\n2228:             \"key_files\": [\"review/review-report.md\"]\n2229:           }\n2230: \n2231:       step_generate_context:\n2232:         action: \"Route continuity content into the correct canonical spec document via generate-context.js\"\n2233:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2234:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js /tmp/save-context-data-<session-id>.json {spec_folder} --full-auto\"\n2235:         critical_rule: \"NEVER manually author files under retired memory/ paths (the runtime rejects them); use generate-context.js so the save routes into decision-record.md, implementation-summary.md, or handover.md\"\n2236: \n2237:       step_verify_save:\n2238:         action: \"Verify canonical save routed content into the correct spec document\"\n2239:         check: \"Does {spec_folder}/implementation-summary.md, {spec_folder}/decision-record.md, or {spec_folder}/handover.md carry the new continuity update?\"\n2240:         on_fail: \"Log warning but do not block completion\"\n2241: \n2242:       step_release_lock:\n2243:         action: \"Release the single-writer lock after save, skip-save, or cancellation cleanup has resolved\"\n2244:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2245:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}\"\n2246:         bookkeeping_log: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"lock_released\",\"path\":\"{state_paths.lock_file}\",\"releasePhase\":\"save\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n2247: \n2248:   # ════════\n2249:   # COMPLETION\n2250:   # ════════\n2251:   completion:\n2252:     message: |\n2253:       Deep review complete.\n2254:       Iterations: {iteration_count} | Stop reason: {reason}\n2255:       Findings: P0={active_p0} P1={active_p1} P2={active_p2}\n2256:       Verdict: {verdict} | hasAdvisories={has_advisories}\n2257: \n2258:       Artifacts:\n2259:         - review/review-report.md (compiled from {iteration_count} iterations)\n2260:         - {iteration_count} iteration files in review/iterations/\n2261:         - State files in review/: deep-review-config.json, deep-review-state.jsonl, deep-review-findings-registry.json, deep-review-strategy.md, deep-review-dashboard.md\n2262:         - Memory context saved\n2263: \n2264:       STATUS=OK PATH={spec_folder}\n2265:     next_steps:\n2266:       - \"/speckit:plan [remediation] (if FAIL or CONDITIONAL verdict)\"\n2267:       - \"/create:changelog (if PASS, including PASS with hasAdvisories=true)\"\n2268:       - \"/deep:review [target] (for another review)\"\n2269:       - \"/speckit:save {spec_folder} (refresh canonical continuity before the next session)\"\n2270: \n2271: # ────────\n2272: # ERROR RECOVERY\n2273: # ────────\n2274: error_recovery:\n2275:   agent_dispatch_timeout: \"Retry once with reduced scope (fewer files per iteration). If second timeout, mark as 'timeout' and continue.\"\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 2276]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\":200,\"offset\":2076,\"path\":\".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml\"}"},"time":{"start":1794857494895,"end":1794857495319}}}}
