{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794857722875,"sessionID":"ses_e1a303973ffeu6SRRIvgAvpDYA","part":{"partID":"prt_1e5db2166001abiwmidOQMtbDj","sessionID":"ses_e1a303973ffeu6SRRIvgAvpDYA","messageID":"msg_1e5db1061001MxbfWGkk0xnWcI","type":"tool","id":"call_a3ece445d97941cfb74223d4","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"---\ntitle: Deep Review Strategy - command mention pass twelve\ndescription: Runtime strategy for the mention-12 lineage, tracking the commandOnlyMentioned wrapper, quote and alias guards and their invariance test.\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: planning\n---\n\n# Deep Review Strategy - mention-12\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nPersistent state for the `mention-12` lineage of review pass twelve. It records which dimensions remain, what was found, which approaches worked, and where the next iteration focuses.\n\n### Usage\n\n- **Init:** populated from the review brief, the scope file and the commit range.\n- **Per iteration:** read Next Focus, review the named area, record findings, mark dimensions, set the next focus.\n- **Mutability:** updated in place by this lineage.\n\n---\n\n## 2. TOPIC\n\nReview of the mention area for command surfacing pass twelve: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` and `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`. The area covers `commandOnlyMentioned`, which now drops a single quote that opens or closes a command name, keeps an apostrophe inside a word, and reads a retired command name beside the command it maps to, plus the wrapper invariance test that checks every mention fixture reads the same wrapped in code, quote or bold marks, or under the retired name, as plain.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n- [ ] D1 Correctness, Logic errors, off-by-one, wrong return types, broken invariants\n- [ ] D2 Security, Injection, auth bypass, secrets exposure, unsafe deserialization\n- [ ] D3 Traceability, Spec/code alignment, checklist evidence, cross-reference integrity\n- [ ] D4 Maintainability, Patterns, clarity, documentation quality, safe follow-on change cost\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- Reviewing the merged area (`sk-doc/ROUTER.md`, `sk-doc/SKILL.md`, `sk-doc/graph-metadata.json`, the doctor install contract test) assigned to `merged-12`; read-only context only.\n- Re-reporting the recorded limits in `review-brief-12.txt` unless a new input breaks them.\n- Reviewing `typedCommandIn`'s retired-name mapping as new work beyond its interaction with the mention guard.\n- Running the repository test suite, the build, or any git write; this lineage reports only.\n- Opening the prompt corpora except through the allowed aggregate paths; the holdout rule stays in force.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Composite convergence stop at threshold 0.10 with all four dimensions covered.\n- `maxIterations` 8 reached without a legal convergence stop.\n- A blocking stop from `convergence.cjs` naming an uncovered dimension or an unresolved active P0.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n\n| Dimension | Verdict | Iteration | Summary |\n|-----------|---------|-----------|---------|\n| [None yet] | - | - | - |\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\n- **P0 (Critical):** 0 active\n- **P1 (Major):** 0 active\n- **P2 (Minor):** 0 active\n- **Delta this iteration:** +0 P0, +0 P1, +0 P2\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Init: read the brief, the scope file, the two scope files and the pass-ten/pass-eleven reports before choosing a focus; the prior reports name the single-quote and retired-name fixes this pass must test.\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- Init: none.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n\n[None yet]\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Swept: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n\n---\n\n## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n\n[None yet]\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 12. NEXT FOCUS\n- Dimension: correctness and traceability\n- Focus area: `commandOnlyMentioned` normalization and the wrapper invariance test\n- Reason: initialization had one focus to prove: whether a wrapper the test does not cover can change a refusal or question into a request.\n- Rotation status: first pass.\n- Productive carry-forward: the exported function, the fixture rows and the six wrapper pairs.\n- Required evidence: file:line in the module and the test, plus a concrete prompt whose attached command differs from the plain form.\n- Recovery note: none.\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\n\n- Target pointers: `command-attach.ts` `commandOnlyMentioned` (line 424), `COMMAND_GAP_WORDS` (line 363), `RETIRED_COMMANDS` (line 217), `typedCommandIn` (line 221); `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` `WRAPPERS` and `PLAIN_ROWS` (lines 175-197).\n- Behavior claims: a prompt that names a command to refuse it or ask about it must not receive the command; markup around the name must not change that reading; a retired name reads as the command it maps to.\n- Prior fixes: pass ten dropped a single quote that opens a command name; pass eleven dropped a closing quote and read the retired name in the mention check; AC-007 pins the wrapper matrix to backtick, straight and curly quote, bold, and the retired name.\n- Consumers: `attachCommand` line 510 (hub routes), `lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1204-1215` (`withholdMentionedCommands`), `typedCommandForTop` line 256 via `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:427`.\n- Review risks: the wrapper matrix is defined by the normalizer, so a wrapper outside it is invisible to the test; the occurrence regex has a different boundary rule than `typedCommandIn`.\n- Out of scope: the merged area, the scorer weights, and the broad routing accuracy suite; context only.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-reference-status -->\n## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n[Alignment checks completed across core and overlay protocols]\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n|----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n| `spec_code` | core | pending | - | - |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | - | - |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-reference-status -->\n## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n\n| File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\n|------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | - | - | - | pending |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | - | - | - | pending |\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:review-boundaries -->\n## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\n\n- Max iterations: 8\n- Convergence threshold: 0.10\n- Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\n- No-progress threshold: 0.05\n- Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\n- Session lineage: sessionId=fanout-mention-12-1794856957949-n58dw7, parentSessionId=null, generation=1, lineageMode=new\n- Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\n- Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\n- Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 10 minutes\n- Severity threshold: P2\n- Review target type: spec-folder\n- Cross-reference checks: core=[spec_code, checklist_evidence], overlay=[skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability]\n- Started: 2026-11-16T19:34:48Z\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:review-boundaries -->\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-12/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-12/deep-review-strategy.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-12/deep-review-strategy.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"---\\ntitle: Deep Review Strategy - command mention pass twelve\\ndescription: Runtime strategy for the mention-12 lineage, tracking the commandOnlyMentioned wrapper, quote and alias guards and their invariance test.\\nimportance_tier: normal\\ncontextType: planning\\n---\\n\\n# Deep Review Strategy - mention-12\\n\\n## 1. OVERVIEW\\n\\n### Purpose\\n\\nPersistent state for the `mention-12` lineage of review pass twelve. It records which dimensions remain, what was found, which approaches worked, and where the next iteration focuses.\\n\\n### Usage\\n\\n- **Init:** populated from the review brief, the scope file and the commit range.\\n- **Per iteration:** read Next Focus, review the named area, record findings, mark dimensions, set the next focus.\\n- **Mutability:** updated in place by this lineage.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. TOPIC\\n\\nReview of the mention area for command surfacing pass twelve: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` and `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`. The area covers `commandOnlyMentioned`, which now drops a single quote that opens or closes a command name, keeps an apostrophe inside a word, and reads a retired command name beside the command it maps to, plus the wrapper invariance test that checks every mention fixture reads the same wrapped in code, quote or bold marks, or under the retired name, as plain.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\\n- [ ] D1 Correctness, Logic errors, off-by-one, wrong return types, broken invariants\\n- [ ] D2 Security, Injection, auth bypass, secrets exposure, unsafe deserialization\\n- [ ] D3 Traceability, Spec/code alignment, checklist evidence, cross-reference integrity\\n- [ ] D4 Maintainability, Patterns, clarity, documentation quality, safe follow-on change cost\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\\n## 4. NON-GOALS\\n\\n- Reviewing the merged area (`sk-doc/ROUTER.md`, `sk-doc/SKILL.md`, `sk-doc/graph-metadata.json`, the doctor install contract test) assigned to `merged-12`; read-only context only.\\n- Re-reporting the recorded limits in `review-brief-12.txt` unless a new input breaks them.\\n- Reviewing `typedCommandIn`'s retired-name mapping as new work beyond its interaction with the mention guard.\\n- Running the repository test suite, the build, or any git write; this lineage reports only.\\n- Opening the prompt corpora except through the allowed aggregate paths; the holdout rule stays in force.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\\n\\n- Composite convergence stop at threshold 0.10 with all four dimensions covered.\\n- `maxIterations` 8 reached without a legal convergence stop.\\n- A blocking stop from `convergence.cjs` naming an uncovered dimension or an unresolved active P0.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\\n## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\\n\\n| Dimension | Verdict | Iteration | Summary |\\n|-----------|---------|-----------|---------|\\n| [None yet] | - | - | - |\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\\n<!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\\n## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\\n- **P0 (Critical):** 0 active\\n- **P1 (Major):** 0 active\\n- **P2 (Minor):** 0 active\\n- **Delta this iteration:** +0 P0, +0 P1, +0 P2\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n- Init: read the brief, the scope file, the two scope files and the pass-ten/pass-eleven reports before choosing a focus; the prior reports name the single-quote and retired-name fixes this pass must test.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- Init: none.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\\n\\n[None yet]\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\\n- Completed pivots: 0\\n- Failed pivots: 0\\n- Audited overrides: 0\\n- Swept: none yet\\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\\n\\n[None yet]\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n## 12. NEXT FOCUS\\n- Dimension: correctness and traceability\\n- Focus area: `commandOnlyMentioned` normalization and the wrapper invariance test\\n- Reason: initialization had one focus to prove: whether a wrapper the test does not cover can change a refusal or question into a request.\\n- Rotation status: first pass.\\n- Productive carry-forward: the exported function, the fixture rows and the six wrapper pairs.\\n- Required evidence: file:line in the module and the test, plus a concrete prompt whose attached command differs from the plain form.\\n- Recovery note: none.\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\\n\\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\\n\\n- Target pointers: `command-attach.ts` `commandOnlyMentioned` (line 424), `COMMAND_GAP_WORDS` (line 363), `RETIRED_COMMANDS` (line 217), `typedCommandIn` (line 221); `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` `WRAPPERS` and `PLAIN_ROWS` (lines 175-197).\\n- Behavior claims: a prompt that names a command to refuse it or ask about it must not receive the command; markup around the name must not change that reading; a retired name reads as the command it maps to.\\n- Prior fixes: pass ten dropped a single quote that opens a command name; pass eleven dropped a closing quote and read the retired name in the mention check; AC-007 pins the wrapper matrix to backtick, straight and curly quote, bold, and the retired name.\\n- Consumers: `attachCommand` line 510 (hub routes), `lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1204-1215` (`withholdMentionedCommands`), `typedCommandForTop` line 256 via `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:427`.\\n- Review risks: the wrapper matrix is defined by the normalizer, so a wrapper outside it is invisible to the test; the occurrence regex has a different boundary rule than `typedCommandIn`.\\n- Out of scope: the merged area, the scorer weights, and the broad routing accuracy suite; context only.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-reference-status -->\\n## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\\n[Alignment checks completed across core and overlay protocols]\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\\n|----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\\n| `spec_code` | core | pending | - | - |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | - | - |\\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pending | - | - |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pending | - | - |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | - | - |\\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | pending | - | - |\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-reference-status -->\\n## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\\n\\n| File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\\n|------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | - | - | - | pending |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | - | - | - | pending |\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:review-boundaries -->\\n## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\\n\\n- Max iterations: 8\\n- Convergence threshold: 0.10\\n- Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\\n- No-progress threshold: 0.05\\n- Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\\n- Session lineage: sessionId=fanout-mention-12-1794856957949-n58dw7, parentSessionId=null, generation=1, lineageMode=new\\n- Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\\n- Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\\n- Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 10 minutes\\n- Severity threshold: P2\\n- Review target type: spec-folder\\n- Cross-reference checks: core=[spec_code, checklist_evidence], overlay=[skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability]\\n- Started: 2026-11-16T19:34:48Z\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:review-boundaries -->\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-12/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794857705830,"end":1794857722875}}}}
