{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794857827041,"sessionID":"ses_e1a303973ffeu6SRRIvgAvpDYA","part":{"partID":"prt_1e5dcdca6001BD0HXdGOxg2VOe","sessionID":"ses_e1a303973ffeu6SRRIvgAvpDYA","messageID":"msg_1e5dccdb8001OzDKqQ5HiWbLkk","type":"tool","id":"call_95bb7ea1e29544ab958379f0","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Init: read the brief, the scope file, the two scope files and the pass-ten/pass-eleven reports before choosing a focus; the prior reports name the single-quote and retired-name fixes this pass must test.\n- Iteration 1: exercising the module's exported `commandOnlyMentioned` over the test's own `PLAIN_ROWS` instead of only reading the assertions. That drove the wrapper matrix through the real normalizer and lead tests, so the flip is reproduced rather than argued.\n- Iteration 1: reading the occurrence scan and the lead tests separately. It showed the bracketed name is found and the lead is lost, which separated F001 (strip list) from F002 (occurrence boundary) instead of merging them.\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- Init: none.\n- Iteration 1: a first read treated the invariance test's \"every fixture\" comment as full coverage; it is full coverage of the six listed marks only. The wrapper set is the boundary, not the fixture list.\n- Iteration 1: the `PLAIN_ROWS` omission of the or-list question, bare-lead, pronoun and later-clause rows looked like a separate coverage gap, but all those rows show 0 mismatches under the covered wrappers, so it was ruled out rather than reported.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n\nNone yet.\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->","oldString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Init: read the brief, the scope file, the two scope files and the pass-ten/pass-eleven reports before choosing a focus; the prior reports name the single-quote and retired-name fixes this pass must test.\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- Init: none.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n\n[None yet]\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-12/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-12/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-12/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-12/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-12/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-12/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -72,21 +72,25 @@\n <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n \n - Init: read the brief, the scope file, the two scope files and the pass-ten/pass-eleven reports before choosing a focus; the prior reports name the single-quote and retired-name fixes this pass must test.\n+- Iteration 1: exercising the module's exported `commandOnlyMentioned` over the test's own `PLAIN_ROWS` instead of only reading the assertions. That drove the wrapper matrix through the real normalizer and lead tests, so the flip is reproduced rather than argued.\n+- Iteration 1: reading the occurrence scan and the lead tests separately. It showed the bracketed name is found and the lead is lost, which separated F001 (strip list) from F002 (occurrence boundary) instead of merging them.\n \n ---\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n \n - Init: none.\n+- Iteration 1: a first read treated the invariance test's \"every fixture\" comment as full coverage; it is full coverage of the six listed marks only. The wrapper set is the boundary, not the fixture list.\n+- Iteration 1: the `PLAIN_ROWS` omission of the or-list question, bare-lead, pronoun and later-clause rows looked like a separate coverage gap, but all those rows show 0 mismatches under the covered wrappers, so it was ruled out rather than reported.\n \n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n ## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n \n-[None yet]\n+None yet.\n \n <!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n ## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n - Completed pivots: 0\n","status":"modified","additions":5,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-12/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n- Init: read the brief, the scope file, the two scope files and the pass-ten/pass-eleven reports before choosing a focus; the prior reports name the single-quote and retired-name fixes this pass must test.\\n- Iteration 1: exercising the module's exported `commandOnlyMentioned` over the test's own `PLAIN_ROWS` instead of only reading the assertions. That drove the wrapper matrix through the real normalizer and lead tests, so the flip is reproduced rather than argued.\\n- Iteration 1: reading the occurrence scan and the lead tests separately. It showed the bracketed name is found and the lead is lost, which separated F001 (strip list) from F002 (occurrence boundary) instead of merging them.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- Init: none.\\n- Iteration 1: a first read treated the invariance test's \\\"every fixture\\\" comment as full coverage; it is full coverage of the six listed marks only. The wrapper set is the boundary, not the fixture list.\\n- Iteration 1: the `PLAIN_ROWS` omission of the or-list question, bare-lead, pronoun and later-clause rows looked like a separate coverage gap, but all those rows show 0 mismatches under the covered wrappers, so it was ruled out rather than reported.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\\n\\nNone yet.\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\",\"oldString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n- Init: read the brief, the scope file, the two scope files and the pass-ten/pass-eleven reports before choosing a focus; the prior reports name the single-quote and retired-name fixes this pass must test.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- Init: none.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\\n\\n[None yet]\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-12/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794857819302,"end":1794857827041}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794857827052,"sessionID":"ses_e1a303973ffeu6SRRIvgAvpDYA","part":{"partID":"prt_1e5dce842001xhfKcEjZNZ8Fv0","sessionID":"ses_e1a303973ffeu6SRRIvgAvpDYA","messageID":"msg_1e5dccdb8001OzDKqQ5HiWbLkk","type":"tool","id":"call_4558f39ea089473ea6d1047c","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n\n- ReDoS in the lead patterns: a 2,025-character or-list prompt evaluates in 1.2 ms and a 2,425-character alternating list in 0.1 ms (iteration 1).\n- The invariance test's omission of the or-list question, bare-lead, pronoun and later-clause rows from `PLAIN_ROWS`: all those rows show 0 mismatches under the six covered wrappers (iteration 1).\n- A broken single-quote or retired-name fix: both still read refusals, questions and requests as pass eleven recorded (iteration 1).\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 12. NEXT FOCUS\n- Dimension: security and maintainability\n- Focus area: the untrusted-prompt surface of the mention guard, and the two divergent \"is this command named\" boundary rules (`commandOnlyMentioned` normalization versus `typedCommandIn`'s start boundary).\n- Reason: iteration 1 closed correctness and traceability with F001 and F002; security has not checked the guard's regex construction, and maintainability owns the boundary divergence that lets a typed but bold-wrapped command lose delivery.\n- Rotation status: correctness and traceability complete; security and maintainability next.\n- Productive carry-forward: running the exported functions over concrete prompts, then checking the consumer.\n- Required evidence: a `file:line` for the boundary constants and a concrete prompt whose `attachCommand` or `typedCommandForTop` result differs between a wrapped and a plain typed command.\n- Recovery note: none.\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->","oldString":"## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n\n[None yet]\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 12. NEXT FOCUS\n- Dimension: correctness and traceability\n- Focus area: `commandOnlyMentioned` normalization and the wrapper invariance test\n- Reason: initialization had one focus to prove: whether a wrapper the test does not cover can change a refusal or question into a request.\n- Rotation status: first pass.\n- Productive carry-forward: the exported function, the fixture rows and the six wrapper pairs.\n- Required evidence: file:line in the module and the test, plus a concrete prompt whose attached command differs from the plain form.\n- Recovery note: none.\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-12/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-12/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-12/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-12/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-12/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-12/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -103,20 +103,22 @@\n ---\n \n ## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n \n-[None yet]\n+- ReDoS in the lead patterns: a 2,025-character or-list prompt evaluates in 1.2 ms and a 2,425-character alternating list in 0.1 ms (iteration 1).\n+- The invariance test's omission of the or-list question, bare-lead, pronoun and later-clause rows from `PLAIN_ROWS`: all those rows show 0 mismatches under the six covered wrappers (iteration 1).\n+- A broken single-quote or retired-name fix: both still read refusals, questions and requests as pass eleven recorded (iteration 1).\n \n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n ## 12. NEXT FOCUS\n-- Dimension: correctness and traceability\n-- Focus area: `commandOnlyMentioned` normalization and the wrapper invariance test\n-- Reason: initialization had one focus to prove: whether a wrapper the test does not cover can change a refusal or question into a request.\n-- Rotation status: first pass.\n-- Productive carry-forward: the exported function, the fixture rows and the six wrapper pairs.\n-- Required evidence: file:line in the module and the test, plus a concrete prompt whose attached command differs from the plain form.\n+- Dimension: security and maintainability\n+- Focus area: the untrusted-prompt surface of the mention guard, and the two divergent \"is this command named\" boundary rules (`commandOnlyMentioned` normalization versus `typedCommandIn`'s start boundary).\n+- Reason: iteration 1 closed correctness and traceability with F001 and F002; security has not checked the guard's regex construction, and maintainability owns the boundary divergence that lets a typed but bold-wrapped command lose delivery.\n+- Rotation status: correctness and traceability complete; security and maintainability next.\n+- Productive carry-forward: running the exported functions over concrete prompts, then checking the consumer.\n+- Required evidence: a `file:line` for the boundary constants and a concrete prompt whose `attachCommand` or `typedCommandForTop` result differs between a wrapped and a plain typed command.\n - Recovery note: none.\n \n <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n ## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n","status":"modified","additions":9,"deletions":7}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-12/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newStri