{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794858077611,"sessionID":"ses_e1a303973ffeu6SRRIvgAvpDYA","part":{"partID":"prt_1e5e0cc5500249L7MPhZqtJvLW","sessionID":"ses_e1a303973ffeu6SRRIvgAvpDYA","messageID":"msg_1e5e0c6010018Hrae2goeTG670","type":"tool","id":"call_17745c64045e4498990507f5","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-12/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-12/deep-review-strategy.md, lines 1-181\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Review Strategy - command mention pass twelve\n3: description: Runtime strategy for the mention-12 lineage, tracking the commandOnlyMentioned wrapper, quote and alias guards and their invariance test.\n4: importance_tier: normal\n5: contextType: planning\n6: ---\n7: \n8: # Deep Review Strategy - mention-12\n9: \n10: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n11: \n12: ### Purpose\n13: \n14: Persistent state for the `mention-12` lineage of review pass twelve. It records which dimensions remain, what was found, which approaches worked, and where the next iteration focuses.\n15: \n16: ### Usage\n17: \n18: - **Init:** populated from the review brief, the scope file and the commit range.\n19: - **Per iteration:** read Next Focus, review the named area, record findings, mark dimensions, set the next focus.\n20: - **Mutability:** updated in place by this lineage.\n21: \n22: ---\n23: \n24: ## 2. TOPIC\n25: \n26: Review of the mention area for command surfacing pass twelve: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` and `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`. The area covers `commandOnlyMentioned`, which now drops a single quote that opens or closes a command name, keeps an apostrophe inside a word, and reads a retired command name beside the command it maps to, plus the wrapper invariance test that checks every mention fixture reads the same wrapped in code, quote or bold marks, or under the retired name, as plain.\n27: \n28: ---\n29: \n30: <!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n31: ## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n32: - [ ] security\n33: - [ ] maintainability\n34: \n35: <!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n36: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n37: \n38: - Reviewing the merged area (`sk-doc/ROUTER.md`, `sk-doc/SKILL.md`, `sk-doc/graph-metadata.json`, the doctor install contract test) assigned to `merged-12`; read-only context only.\n39: - Re-reporting the recorded limits in `review-brief-12.txt` unless a new input breaks them.\n40: - Reviewing `typedCommandIn`'s retired-name mapping as new work beyond its interaction with the mention guard.\n41: - Running the repository test suite, the build, or any git write; this lineage reports only.\n42: - Opening the prompt corpora except through the allowed aggregate paths; the holdout rule stays in force.\n43: \n44: ---\n45: \n46: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n47: \n48: - Composite convergence stop at threshold 0.10 with all four dimensions covered.\n49: - `maxIterations` 8 reached without a legal convergence stop.\n50: - A blocking stop from `convergence.cjs` naming an uncovered dimension or an unresolved active P0.\n51: \n52: ---\n53: \n54: <!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n55: ## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n56: - [x] correctness\n57: - [x] traceability\n58: \n59: <!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n60: <!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n61: ## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n62: - P0 (Blockers): 0\n63: - P1 (Required): 1\n64: - P2 (Suggestions): 1\n65: - Resolved: 0\n66: \n67: <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n68: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n69: \n70: - Init: read the brief, the scope file, the two scope files and the pass-ten/pass-eleven reports before choosing a focus; the prior reports name the single-quote and retired-name fixes this pass must test.\n71: - Iteration 1: exercising the module's exported `commandOnlyMentioned` over the test's own `PLAIN_ROWS` instead of only reading the assertions. That drove the wrapper matrix through the real normalizer and lead tests, so the flip is reproduced rather than argued.\n72: - Iteration 1: reading the occurrence scan and the lead tests separately. It showed the bracketed name is found and the lead is lost, which separated F001 (strip list) from F002 (occurrence boundary) instead of merging them.\n73: \n74: ---\n75: \n76: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n77: \n78: - Init: none.\n79: - Iteration 1: a first read treated the invariance test's \"every fixture\" comment as full coverage; it is full coverage of the six listed marks only. The wrapper set is the boundary, not the fixture list.\n80: - Iteration 1: the `PLAIN_ROWS` omission of the or-list question, bare-lead, pronoun and later-clause rows looked like a separate coverage gap, but all those rows show 0 mismatches under the covered wrappers, so it was ruled out rather than reported.\n81: \n82: ---\n83: \n84: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n85: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n86: ### A missing occurrence of a bracketed name: the scan finds the name inside `[...]`; only the lead fails. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n87: - What was tried: A missing occurrence of a bracketed name: the scan finds the name inside `[...]`; only the lead fails.\n88: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n89: - Do NOT retry: A missing occurrence of a bracketed name: the scan finds the name inside `[...]`; only the lead fails.\n90: \n91: ### A regression from the single-quote or retired-name fixes: both still behave as pass eleven recorded. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n92: - What was tried: A regression from the single-quote or retired-name fixes: both still behave as pass eleven recorded.\n93: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n94: - Do NOT retry: A regression from the single-quote or retired-name fixes: both still behave as pass eleven recorded.\n95: \n96: ### ReDoS in the lead patterns: a 2,025-character or-list prompt evaluates in 1.2 ms and a 2,425-character alternating list in 0.1 ms; the anchored alternation does not backtrack catastrophically at these sizes. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n97: - What was tried: ReDoS in the lead patterns: a 2,025-character or-list prompt evaluates in 1.2 ms and a 2,425-character alternating list in 0.1 ms; the anchored alternation does not backtrack catastrophically at these sizes.\n98: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n99: - Do NOT retry: ReDoS in the lead patterns: a 2,025-character or-list prompt evaluates in 1.2 ms and a 2,425-character alternating list in 0.1 ms; the anchored alternation does not backtrack catastrophically at these sizes.\n100: \n101: ### The test's omission of the or-list question, bare-lead, pronoun and later-clause rows from `PLAIN_ROWS`: all of those rows still show 0 mismatches under the six covered wrappers, so the omission is not hiding a second defect today. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n102: - What was tried: The test's omission of the or-list question, bare-lead, pronoun and later-clause rows from `PLAIN_ROWS`: all of those rows still show 0 mismatches under the six covered wrappers, so the omission is not hiding a second defect today.\n103: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n104: - Do NOT retry: The test's omission of the or-list question, bare-lead, pronoun and later-clause rows from `PLAIN_ROWS`: all of those rows still show 0 mismatches under the six covered wrappers, so the omission is not hiding a second defect today.\n105: \n106: <!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n107: ## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n108: - Completed pivots: 0\n109: - Failed pivots: 0\n110: - Audited overrides: 0\n111: - Swept: none yet\n112: - Pivot lineage: none yet\n113: - Remaining frontier: none recorded\n114: \n115: ## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\