{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794858110549,"sessionID":"ses_e1a303973ffeu6SRRIvgAvpDYA","part":{"partID":"prt_1e5e13253001nguz5Cnzdajhlm","sessionID":"ses_e1a303973ffeu6SRRIvgAvpDYA","messageID":"msg_1e5e12aaa001WuCCtbwnbcxwWt","type":"tool","id":"call_bf2c5f2382b64c47a2515ab1","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n- Dimension: all four, as a final cross-reference and verification pass\n- Focus area: re-run the F001, F002 and F003 prompts from the final tree, recheck the recorded limits, and prove the lineage state (iteration files, deltas, state log, registry, strategy) agrees before synthesis.\n- Reason: all four dimensions are covered; no P0 exists and F001 is the only active P1, so the next pass verifies rather than discovers.\n- Rotation status: exhausted for discovery; verification only.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: the exported-function probe method used in iterations 1 and 2.\n- Required evidence: the same prompts, plus the convergence script's stop decision recorded in the state log.\n- Recovery note: none.\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->","oldString":"<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n- Dimension: security and maintainability - Focus area: the untrusted-prompt surface of the mention guard, and the two divergent \"is this command named\" boundary rules (`commandOnlyMentioned` normalization versus `typedCommandIn`'s start boundary). - Reason: correctness produced the wrapper flip and the path occurrence; security has not yet checked the guard's regex construction, and maintainability owns the boundary divergence that lets a typed but bold-wrapped command lose its delivery. - Rotation status: first pass complete for correctness and traceability; security and maintainability next. - Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive was exercising the exported module over the test's own fixtures; keep that method for the typed boundary. - Required evidence: a `file:line` for the boundary constants and a concrete prompt whose `attachCommand` or `typedCommandForTop` result differs between a wrapped and a plain typed command. - Recovery note: none. Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-12/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-12/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-12/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-12/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-12/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/mention-12/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -128,9 +128,15 @@\n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n-- Dimension: security and maintainability - Focus area: the untrusted-prompt surface of the mention guard, and the two divergent \"is this command named\" boundary rules (`commandOnlyMentioned` normalization versus `typedCommandIn`'s start boundary). - Reason: correctness produced the wrapper flip and the path occurrence; security has not yet checked the guard's regex construction, and maintainability owns the boundary divergence that lets a typed but bold-wrapped command lose its delivery. - Rotation status: first pass complete for correctness and traceability; security and maintainability next. - Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive was exercising the exported module over the test's own fixtures; keep that 