moglyph, zero-width or fullwidth command form as a guard bypass: it does not name a tracked command, so no route selects the command (iteration 2).\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n- Dimension: all four, as a final cross-reference and verification pass - Focus area: verify F001, F002 and F003 still reproduce from the final tree, recheck the recorded limits, and prove the lineage state (iteration file, delta, state log, registry, strategy) agrees before synthesis. - Reason: security and maintainability are closed; no P0 exists and the active P1 is F001, so the next pass is verification rather than another discovery angle. - Rotation status: all four dimensions will be covered after this pass. - Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive was exercising the exported functions over concrete prompts; carry that into the final recheck. - Required evidence: the same prompts used in iterations 1 and 2, plus the convergence script's stop decision recorded in the state log. - Recovery note: none. Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\n\n- Target pointers: `command-attach.ts` `commandOnlyMentioned` (line 424), `COMMAND_GAP_WORDS` (line 363), `RETIRED_COMMANDS` (line 217), `typedCommandIn` (line 221); `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` `WRAPPERS` and `PLAIN_ROWS` (lines 175-197).\n- Behavior claims: a prompt that names a command to refuse it or ask about it must not receive the command; markup around the name must not change that reading; a retired name reads as the command it maps to.\n- Prior fixes: pass ten dropped a single quote that opens a command name; pass eleven dropped a closing quote and read the retired name in the mention check; AC-007 pins the wrapper matrix to backtick, straight and curly quote, bold, and the retired name.\n- Consumers: `attachCommand` line 510 (hub routes), `lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1204-1215` (`withholdMentionedCommands`), `typedCommandForTop` line 256 via `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:427`.\n- Review risks: the wrapper matrix is defined by the normalizer, so a wrapper outside it is invisible to the test; the occurrence regex has a different boundary rule than `typedCommandIn`.\n- Out of scope: the merged area, the scorer weights, and the broad routing accuracy suite; context only.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-reference-status -->\n## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n[Alignment checks completed across core and overlay protocols]\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n|----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n| `spec_code` | core | pass | 1 | The branch diff is the two scope files and does what pass eleven's report says; F001 and F002 are new defects outside AC-007's enumerated marks. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | notApplicable | 1 | No packet checklist belongs to this review pass; 039 AC-007 was read as the wrapper contract and is met as written. |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pass | 1 | No agent definition is in the diff. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | notApplicable | 1 | No runtime mirror is touched by the scope files. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | partial | 2 | The wrapper test pins the six listed marks; F001 names the class it cannot see, F002 the occurrence-boundary disagreement, and F003 the second wrapper implementation in the typed path. |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | partial | 2 | No playbook scenario executed; the exported functions were exercised directly with the fixture rows, the uncovered wrappers and the large-prompt probes. |\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-reference-status -->\n## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n\n| File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\n|------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | D1, D2, D3, D4 | 2 | 1 P1, 2 P2 | partial |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | D1, D3, D4 |